File: /Volumes/Attic/Desktop/Projects/crates/oscore/src/edhoc/kdf.rs
Lines: 62-74

CBOR bstr encoding only handles context up to 255 bytes:
```rust
} else if context.len() <= 255 {
    info.push_err(0x58)?;
    info.push_err(context.len() as u8)?;
    info.extend_err(context)?;
} else {
    return Err(EdhocError::BufferTooSmall);
}
```

CBOR supports longer bstrings (0x59 for 2-byte length), but the error returned is BufferTooSmall which is misleading.

This is acceptable for EDHOC (TH is 32 bytes) but should be documented:
1. Add doc comment stating 255-byte context limit
2. Consider a more descriptive error variant (ContextTooLong)
